f(\mathbf{x}) := \frac{1}{n}\sum_{i=1}^n f_i(\mathbf{x})
\end{align} 
is a smooth loss function over $n$ training samples that describes the fitness to data, and the second term $g$ is a nonsmooth regularization function that encodes \emph{a priori} information.

